# ::tok Nonetheless, the persistence of wage growth is unlikely to reverse the current rapid decline in inflation, with the M2 data turning negative year on year and leading CPI indicators gradually improving, and the US CPI data having shifted to a rapid decline since October. The persistence of wage growth will only underpin future inflation data, and current market expectations will be hard to disprove, and the market will enter a new round of games once inflation data are released.
